1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,700
Could that be automatic? Like the screen just opens?

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:11,700
You want me to say yes. I can't prove that.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,920
I'm not asking you to prove it. Could it happen?

4
00:00:18,220 --> 00:00:21,750
And then you write that I said it could.

5
00:00:22,050 --> 00:00:23,230
I'd check it.

6
00:00:23,530 --> 00:00:26,270
You were going to check last time.

7
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:41,700
I told you I hadn't seen the logs. You wrote it down.

8
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:45,300
I thought three cases was enough.

9
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:51,920
Enough for what? I gave you three cases to check.

10
00:00:52,220 --> 00:00:54,180
The same thing kept happening.

11
00:00:54,480 --> 00:00:59,190
Then write that. You didn't need to make me say the rest.

12
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:12,300
They pulled the follow-up.

13
00:01:12,600 --> 00:01:16,400
I have to answer this in the morning.

14
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:24,750
I can explain that you warned me.

15
00:01:25,050 --> 00:01:29,360
To who? Your editor? The people asking me for every message?

16
00:01:29,660 --> 00:01:30,840
In the correction.

17
00:01:31,140 --> 00:01:35,060
Then write it. Don't ask me to fix it first.

18
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:46,300
What can I use?

19
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:49,900
Use what I actually told you.

20
00:01:53,300 --> 00:01:58,350
Cut 'was misunderstood.' What did you get wrong?

21
00:01:58,900 --> 00:02:04,450
I wrote, 'Nobody opened the files.' I can't back that up.

22
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:12,140
We still don't know whether they read everything.

23
00:02:12,440 --> 00:02:18,320
Say that after the correction. Don't use it to get around what we do know.

24
00:02:18,620 --> 00:02:22,150
Okay. Someone accessed the page. My sentence was wrong.

25
00:02:31,300 --> 00:02:38,850
We're holding your next assignment. Legal needs your notes and source files tonight.

26
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:43,450
My name stays on the correction?

27
00:02:47,300 --> 00:02:50,850
Yes. Are you ready?

28
00:02:51,400 --> 00:02:54,950
Send it. Leave my name on.

29
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:13,000
Lena, it's Nora. The correction's up. I've still got questions about your report. Call me when you can.

30
00:03:15,300 --> 00:03:20,350
You didn't say that. I put it in the story. I'm sorry.

31
00:03:20,900 --> 00:03:25,450
My lawyer said you'd come back for another quote.

32
00:03:29,300 --> 00:03:39,850
I've got an interview Monday. I need to get back to work. I'm not doing this again.

33
00:03:43,300 --> 00:03:51,350
We can keep this off the record. What did I miss?

34
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:03,310
Nothing from today goes in a story unless we agree later.

35
00:04:03,610 --> 00:04:07,140
Agreed. No recording. I'll ask before I use anything.

36
00:04:07,440 --> 00:04:11,360
Don't contact the places I'm applying to.

37
00:04:11,660 --> 00:04:12,760
I understand.

38
00:04:20,300 --> 00:04:29,850
You copied the date. What about 'attachments: see list'? It's right there in the photo I let you take.

39
00:04:30,400 --> 00:04:32,450
I see it.
